CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1791037074
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sun 18 Oct to Sun 1 NovFThe
OL,6,Fsecond half of October will probably
OL,7,Fmaintain a changeable pattern overall
OL,8,Fwith weather systems often moving in
OL,9,Ffrom the Atlantic. These will bring
OL,10,Fshowers or longer spells of rain, with
OL,11,Fthe wettest and windiest weather in
OL,12,Fthe northwest, drier in the southeast.
OL,13,FThere is a chance that a period of
OL,14,Fmore widely dry conditions could
OL,15,Fdevelop for a time, but confidence in
OL,16,Fthe details of this is low.
OL,17,FTemperatures will probably be above
OL,18,Faverage overall.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
